> I cannot see any difference in meaning yet between "I need a doctor", "I
> need any doctor" and "mi nitcu 1 mikce". The applicable set of doctors and
> lo mikce is the same.

"mi nitcu 1 mikce" == "There is a single doctor that I need".

In English, I just say "I need a doctor" for the "any" sense. It's
still a different thing though.

There's also the point that the "lo" stuff claims such a doctor
exists that can satisfy your needs.

